# Source: https://github.com/igvteam/igv/issues/1396
#   https://www.encodeproject.org/data-standards/wgbs/
# Symptom: bedMethyl format (Bismark CX report / modkit output) uses 10 columns:
#   chrom, start, end, name(mod_code), score, strand, thickStart, thickEnd,
#   itemRgb, coverage, percentModified (as 0-100 integer).  When treated as
#   BED6, the extra columns (coverage, percent) shift field indices; tools
#   expecting col 5 to be score 0-1000 receive coverage counts that exceed
#   1000.  Distinct from bismark_methylation.bed (5-col variant).
# Format: chrom start end name score strand thickStart thickEnd itemRgb coverage percentMod
chr1	10000	10001	m	90	+	10000	10001	255,0,0	50	90
chr1	10002	10003	m	0	-	10002	10003	0,0,255	10	0
chr1	10100	10101	m	75	+	10100	10101	127,127,0	200	75
